BandManager.ai Context Folder
==============================

📚 Knowledge Base for Agents, Skills, and Developers
Total: 11 files, ~4,100 lines of documentation

READING ORDER:

1. README.md (this folder's guide)
   └─ Start here for navigation

2. AGENT_CONTEXT.md ⭐ (5 min read)
   └─ Everything an agent needs to know in one page

3. SIMPLICITY_FIRST.md ⭐⭐ (15 min read) [Diego's Obsession]
   └─ Zero-friction UX, 3-second test, complexity detection checklist

4. PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md (10 min)
   └─ What is BandManager.ai? Stack, values, status

5. ARCHITECTURE.md (20 min)
   └─ How it works: dual runtime, data layer, auth, deploy

6. DATABASE_SCHEMA.md (20 min)
   └─ Complete Supabase schema: ER diagram, all tables, RLS, queries

7. SECURITY.md ⚠️ CRITICAL (20 min)
   └─ Trust boundary, multi-tenancy, SSRF, rate limiting

8. BUSINESS_RULES.md (30 min)
   └─ AI agents spec: Scout, Redactor, Enviador, Lector

9. CODE_STANDARDS.md (15 min)
   └─ TypeScript, Backend patterns, Frontend, Testing

10. UI_UX_GUIDELINES.md (15 min)
    └─ Design principles: content-first, responsive, dark mode

11. GLOSSARY.md (reference)
    └─ Terms, acronyms, state machines, critical functions

---

QUICK START:
→ Read AGENT_CONTEXT.md first (5 min, everything linked)
→ Read SIMPLICITY_FIRST.md next (complexity matters most)
→ Then jump to specific files based on your task
→ Always check GLOSSARY.md if you need term definitions

BUILD & RUN:
npm install
npm run dev          # Frontend + Backend (HMR)
npm run build        # Production build
npm start            # Production run
npm test             # Vitest

QUALITY CHECKS:
npm run tsc --noEmit  # Type checking (must pass)
npm run lint          # esbuild dry-run
npm test              # All tests must pass

FILES TO PROTECT:
- SIMPLICITY_FIRST.md  (user rejection prevention, core value)
- SECURITY.md          (security rules, never weaken)
- BUSINESS_RULES.md    (agent lifecycle, human-in-the-loop)
- CODE_STANDARDS.md    (keep baseline 0 TS errors)
- DATABASE_SCHEMA.md   (band_id filters, multi-tenancy)
